# Scope Policy

Core import/export is working. This file is a living deferral list, not an initial-implementation freeze.

## In view — first-party plugins

Closed plugin kinds (see `.cursor/rules/16-plugins.mdc`):

- **projection** — read-only view of IR for templates / CLI / downstream lookup (e.g. map by `logicalId`)
- **writer-filter** — ordered filters on validated Raw (layout defaults, residual restore, derive target-specified info)
- **adapter-target** — in-repo Reader / Writer / Transformer bundle

Allowed now:

- Design and implement the smallest contract + one concrete plugin per kind that has a real caller
- Compose writer-filters as an ordered pipeline (`payload → filter → payload`)
- Inject **ids and order** through static inflow channels: `application.yml`, CLI flags, or optional call arguments. Implement only the channel the first caller needs. Do not freeze the product to a single channel

Still forbidden as a *framework*:

- Runtime load of untrusted / out-of-repo code (`eval`, arbitrary dynamic `import`)
- Third-party plugin SDK, marketplace, sandbox, or lifecycle PluginHost
- Event bus (a filter pipeline is not an event bus)
- A shared Plugin base class covering all kinds before three hosts share the same code
- Empty hosts with no concrete plugin behind them

## Deferred until explicitly requested

| Item | May do locally | Must not build |
|---|---|---|
| Event bus | Direct calls, Context, stores; **ordered filter pipelines** | App-wide pub/sub |
| Domain validation | Boundary Raw Zod; a local IR check when a bug needs it | Generic engine / rule DSL |
| Undo/Redo | Snapshot `current` / `history` / `versions` | Editor command stack |
| IR schema migration | Additive IR changes; snapshot *product* versions (`versions/`) | Format migration engine |
| Service framework | Use-case modules and plugin pipeline runners | Generic application/domain-service layer |

If a task seems to need a deferred item, solve with the smallest local approach that keeps Reader → Raw → validate → IR → GUI (and reverse) working. Projections and writer-filters sit *beside* that flow; they must not replace IR as the SSOT (Single Source Of Truth).
